# 0148 WIP: read-only pwrap dump + explicit PMIF v3 init.
# Patch 0148 builds on 0147.  Adds "pwrap dump" (PMIF v3 registers, no
# writes) and "pwrap init" under a new rubypwrap=1 key.  The real driver is
# mtk-pmic-wrap_v1.c (CONFIG_MTK_PMIC_WRAP=y, mediatek,mt6877-pwrap): the
# bootloader normally initialises the wrapper and the MT6359 SPI slave, and
# pmic_mt6359 has no slave init caps, so "pwrap init" only sets the PMIF
# INIT_DONE bit (0x0) and checks SWINF_2_STA bit15.  It writes no PMIC,
# rail, topckgen or clock-gate register.  Commands and descriptors are
# unchanged.
#
# The test cmdline is the 0146a one plus rubypwrap=1 (rubyep2log=0,
# sweetgt=0, rubyprobe=1, no rubypmic).  v1 (41323619559) failed at the
# mt6885 HAL reset_spislv; v2 (41326148595) added the clock/reset block and
# still failed.  v3 switches to the MT6877 PMIF v3 layout.  CI 41327790354
# built v3 on macos-15/Xcode 16.0; the kernel and image hashes below are
# recorded.  KERNEL_EXPECT_EXEC_DATA stays empty until the device run.
MACOS_VERSION=13.5
KERNEL_CONFIG=DEVELOPMENT
MACHINE_CONFIG=SWEET

